'Vagal Toning Practices':'The vagus nerve is like a calming cable in our body. Humming, singing and slow breathing switch it on.',
'Sensory Overload':'Too much noise, light or crowds can make us feel overwhelmed. Finding a quiet place helps.',
'Widening Your Window':'Little by little, we can learn to handle a bit more stress, like a muscle growing stronger.',
'Daily Regulation Rhythms':'Doing things at the same time each day (sleep, meals, play) helps our body feel safe and steady.',
'Your Personal Regulation Map':'Make your own map: what makes you upset, the signs, and what helps you feel better.',
'Procrastination':'Procrastination is putting things off. Starting with just two minutes makes it easier to begin.',
