'The Anger Iceberg':'Anger is like the tip of an iceberg. Underneath are hurt, fear or sadness. Looking underneath helps us understand.',
'The Behaviour Iceberg':'What people do is the tip of the iceberg. Underneath are their thoughts, feelings and needs.',
'The Perfectionism Iceberg':'Trying to be perfect often hides fear of not being loved. You are loved already.',
'The Anger Volcano':'Anger can build up like a volcano. Noticing the rumble early and cooling down stops it erupting.',
